# Written by hand: a dysfunctional variant of arch1.sheep-out. The plugin cannot break a connector yet:
# to run it, delete the connector sg.bsrc in a copy of the model, then play this scenario on that copy.
scenario: The sheep alert is lost on the way
id: arch1.sheep-alert-lost
kind: dysfunctional
version: 0.1
status: draft
goal: Without the link from Sheep Guard to the base station, a stray sheep is still counted, but the operator is never told.
description: Shows what a broken connector does, and what the nominal scenario would have caught: the missing message, not the states.
author: MBSE Shepherd, to review
date: 2026-11-04
tags: part3, architecture 1, fault
from: arch1.sheep-out

instead of sheep-out:
  step sheep-out-lost: pasture sends Sheep Out Of Zone
    note: A sheep leaves the zone; the connector from Sheep Guard to the base station is broken.
    fault: connector sg.bsrc broken
    then soi.sg is Sheep Counting
    then no message Sheep Exit Alert
